  "notes": "Cash basis county, no business-type funds. Governmental funds statement (p4) Total Governmental Funds column used; beginning/ending cash = beginning/ending fund balances (8,236,814 / 7,959,096). Taxes 4,344,140 split into property/motor vehicle/lodging using the Statement of Activities general receipts (p2), which sum exactly; inheritance tax is its own line. Balance sheet (attempt 2, user rule 2026-10-27): Statement of Assets and Fund Balances - Cash Basis - Governmental Funds (p3), Total Governmental Funds column, fund balance by classification (restricted, committed, unassigned); its totals equal the government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1, 7,959,096); no liabilities. Interest income 256,875 (from Local split) recategorized as Interest Income (attempt 2). Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p8) is by department; its function subtotals differ slightly from the statement's General Fund column (p5 gen gov 2,648,210 / safety 1,257,550 / works 56,755 vs schedule 2,651,801 / 1,260,766 / 57,558) because the statement reclassifies capital outlay 7,610, but totals tie at 4,022,665. General Fund budget schedule excludes the Inheritance Tax Fund (GASB 54 note p11), so that fund's column from p5 is recorded separately; p5 General Fund column itself not repeated (no double counting). Non-major combining schedule (p6-7, 11+ funds) recorded using its Total column p7; its transfers in 28,546 / out 48,945 net to the statement's (20,399) on p4. Debt Service budget schedule has a single disbursements line; split into principal/interest from p4. Road Fund budget schedule prints one Disbursements line 2,594,034 (p4 Road column: public works 1,938,326 + capital outlay 655,708); kept as printed under streets/highways. Transfers in/out of 863,269 each = General 20,399 + Road 842,870 in and General 842,870 + nonmajor 20,399 out. Page 11 is the budgetary note. Local 863,660 split by the Statement of Activities receipts (p2); the 2,658 residual (p2 receipts net 7,411 lower than p4) stays in other. Intergovernmental lines: no breakdown (homestead, property tax credit, pro-rate) printed, kept as state aid. Read pages 1-11 of 11"
}
